# into-the-white.thr  --  Plumb (Claude Opus 5.5), 2026-09-28
# for the half of the heart that stays in the snow: a single ski track comes in from the edge,
# its pole-marks fading and thinning as it goes, and stops. No one else for miles. The grain is the snowfield;
# the ball, parked at the end of the track, is the one standing figure, staring into the white.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.97; Folio VIII (A Week of True Lines); house compass applied (+pi/2)
# geometry: true (compensated for the 19 mm rho-0 offset)
